---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout title="How It Works"><section class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">Growth through faithful practice</span><h1>More than a completed checklist.</h1><p class="lead">Learn with others. Practice real responsibilities. Demonstrate what you can do. Use it to serve—and eventually teach.</p></section><section><div class="journey">{[['Learn','Receive biblical and practical instruction.'],['Practice','Try the skill, repeat it, and receive correction.'],['Demonstrate','Show understanding through a useful task or conversation.'],['Serve','Put your learning to work for someone else.'],['Teach','Help another person grow in what you have learned.']].map(([title,text],i)=><div><span class="number">0{i+1}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{text}</p></div>)}</div></section><section class="two-column"><div><h2>Four pillars</h2><p>Identity, Stewardship, Service, and Dominion bring biblical formation and practical responsibility together.</p><a href={`${base}pillars/`}>Read about the four pillars</a><h2>Three levels</h2><p>Apprentice builds broad foundational experience. Pathfinder develops competence and greater choice. Vanguard grows toward maturity, leadership, service, and teaching.</p><a href={`${base}levels/`}>Explore the three levels</a><h2>Challenges</h2><p>Choose a challenge, read the requirements, arrange adult involvement, and practice. Apprentice challenges are generally required; options within a challenge give different ways to complete it.</p></div><div><h2><Icon name="demonstration"/>Demonstration</h2><p>Completion should be visible in understanding and ability. Explain, show, or carry out the final requirement with someone who can give useful feedback.</p><h2><Icon name="signoff"/>Sign-off</h2><p>An appropriate adult observes or discusses the work and confirms the requirements. Local churches decide who may sign off. This prototype lets participants record readiness, not official approval.</p><h2>The church helps build people</h2><p>Parents, pastors, mentors, and skilled church members invest personally in participants. Foundation Framework creates opportunities for discipleship within the local church.</p><a href={`${base}for-the-church/`}>Find your role</a></div></section></Layout>
